resident evil code veronica is an  overlooked gem of the series and i think  if you've never played it it's about  time you do no matter how much i play  classic resident evil games returning to  them is never a warm and fuzzy  experience it's addicting but terrifying  tight corners zombies jump scares tank  controls and the dread of losing hours  of progression over one mistake but  these were the things that helped rocket  the resident evil series to worldwide  success and even though i was terrified  to sleep most nights after playing i  mean i was like 10 years old i loved  every minute of it in this video i want  to talk about code veronica and why it's  not only so great but important before  the series story went backwards with  resident evil 0 code veronica had  several loose ends to tie up from its  prequels resident evil 1 through 3. in  fact code veronica was almost part 3.  during its development capcom was  transitioning through a new generation  of gaming hardware originally an  exclusive title for the sega dreamcast  code veronica was a result of a failed  resident evil 2 port for the sega saturn  once the developers realized that the  port wouldn't work they shifted to a new  project for the upcoming dreamcast  instead resident evil code veronica  despite the excitement of the all-new  dreamcast making this game an exclusive  title was a hard ask considering the  playstation 2 was just around the corner  soon enough resident evil 4 came along  and changed everything however just  before the dawn of this new  over-the-shoulder action survival era  there were a few games that bid farewell  to the series as we once knew it despite  these games also getting their start on  6th gen hardware they were quickly  overshadowed by resident evil 4 and the  turning point it created for the beloved  capcom series i think for this big  reason code veronica never truly had its  chance to shine in the sun and that  needs to change but first a little  backstory  [Music]  taking place three months after the  events of resident evil 3 nemesis we  catch up with claire redfield still on  the hunt for her missing brother chris  claire ends up in a secluded island  prison run by the umbrella corporation  the events of resident evil 2 have  hardened our protagonist as seen by the  explosive opening where claire dodges  enemy guards and even evades a minigun  mounted to a helicopter a scene reused  in the second resident evil film two  years later  they're the same picture it's a far cry  from resident evil 2's opening where  she's almost eaten and accidentally  killed within the first few minutes  don't shoot down  you okay  boy if you don't some of the biggest  takeaways with code veronica are its  story characters and environments  pulling players away from raccoon city  for the first time is unsettling but  makes for such a memorable experience  from the start despite all the terrors  that lie ahead the environments in code  veronica have held up well over the last  20 years the rockford island prison in  the game's first half is dark and full  of secrets much like the spencer mansion  or the rpd in previous games you soon  figure out that the island is more than  a prison in training ground the prison  belongs to the ashford family a royal  family whose dynasty came to a crumbling  end at rockford  the game's opening isn't all doom and  gloom though that's because code  veronica was blessed with the  introduction of steve burnside a fellow  prisoner escapee shut up claire and  steve find each other at the start of  the game and team up to escape well sort  of  i don't want you following me  steve wears his heart on his sleeve and  you'll never know what you'll get with  each encounter you learn that he and his  father were imprisoned at rockford after  attempting to sell information about an  umbrella to the public his flashy  attitude terrible flirting skills and  tight outfit make him an easy target but  at 17 years old he's just a boy an  emotionally charged boy who runs around  with gaudy golden luger handguns and  telling claire that she can't count on  anyone in this world and that even guns  are more reliable than humans he is a  mess but one i grew to love over the  years or you know love to hate shut up  i don't want to talk about it  in the wii title umbrella chronicles the  story is retold with a more level-headed  steve damn girl which is fine but  underwhelming compared to the steve i  know and love  i so want to enjoy  this  that uh joyful giggle is from none other  than alfred ashford one of the game's  main antagonists his backstory is deep  and disturbing in short he was an  unplanned clone created by his father  alexander alexander created this clone  using dna from a former family matriarch  named veronica to create a prodigy child  and bring back the glory to the ashford  name however during the process he  accidentally created twins alexia and  alfred with notably less intelligence  than his clone sister alfred grew up in  alexia's shadow despite this alfred  worshipped alexia and the two grew up  together at an umbrella antarctic base  in harmony  claire meets alfred with his back  against the wall calling her out for  being a spy and blaming her for the  bombing run on rockford island that had  happened mere moments ago when it was  actually albert wesker that was  responsible  that's right wesker returns in his first  appearance after his death in resident  evil 1. having injected himself with the  strain of the t-virus that night at the  spencer mansion not only was he able to  survive the tyrant attack but he became  a superhuman in the process his role in  code veronica is way more menacing now  that he transcends human strength and  it's also very over the top his  superpowers make him hit harder super  jump and give his eyes a red glow claire  is the real hero here but wesker's  melodramatic performance as a superhuman  is one to remember and who could forget  alexia herself at this point i've  mentioned alexia quite a bit but code  veronica does a great job of building  her up and surrounding her backstory and  mystery now we all know having a clone  sibling in video games doesn't tend to  work out in many cases  and the ashfords are no exception this  awful little uh home movie claire finds  is a 45 second red flag alfred even uses  this as his computer's boot up screen  and the older these two got the worse it  became i won't give away too much  because i really want you to play this  for yourself but let's just say the  relationship between these two is weird  it's just weird  another special appearance is chris  redfield okay i know he's on the cover  of the box but when i first played this  i felt like his arrival would never  happen so it still feels special to me  chris is back and on the hunt for claire  his dramatic opening climbing up  rockford island makes for a badass  return you really start to understand  why he hates rocks  his relationship with wesker rears its  ugly head and code veronica's story  which is a treat despite the two wanting  to kill each other after what happened  in resident evil 1 you guys are idiots  and how could we forget the reunion of  claire and chris  claire began her journey into the  resident evil series with the sole  purpose of finding her brother the  ending of resident evil 2 revealed a lot  about the umbrella corporation the  g-virus raccoon city and its lousy mayor  and way more but while she survived  claire's mission was incomplete and  chris's whereabouts remained unknown the  two finally crossed paths at the  antarctic base and worked together to  try to stop wesker and the ashfords and  contain the new veronica virus  if you played resident evil 1-4 and  skipped code veronica you missed the  first time seeing the redfields together  you blew it  okay now that we've talked about code  veronica's story and main characters  let's talk about the actual gameplay  that also makes this game so great  the theme you're hearing is one of the  most terrifying melodies that represents  alexia and alfred much like resident  evil 2 it's music tracks like this that  are burned into my memory purely  associated with the terror of alfred and  his disturbing family mansion  [Music]  being one of the last classic resident  evil titles the formula of survival  horror with fixed camera perspective has  really been polished here and has aged  very well in a post resident evil 4  world  the puzzles aren't too hard which lets  you focus on surviving and the story but  they're peppered in just enough to break  up the gameplay like before all the  files and diaries found can nudge you in  the right direction if you're feeling a  little lost  now between you and me i remember going  into a gamestop and finding one answer  to a puzzle that i was looking for that  had boggled me for weeks after i found  the answer i was looking for i left  without buying the guide and i felt like  i robbed the place  and i remember writing down this stolen  intel in my game's manual which i still  have  wow richie that puzzle wasn't hard at  all couldn't figure that one out on your  own bud  little known fact this was the last  resident evil title that included  weapons using their real world names  like the ak-47 and calico m100  submachine gun some were modified and  not all of these are entirely accurate  but cool nonetheless thanks time morgan  ink ribbon all that being said this  game's a little hard i personally  remember putting this game down for  quite a while because i simply couldn't  get through it now i know i'm not the  best resident evil player but while most  agree that it's not necessarily easy  it's definitely worth it there's also  this unlockable mode called battle game  that lets you take revenge on every  living creature this game has to offer  you can play as claire steve chris and  for the first time you can even play as  wesker after revisiting this mode years  later i have to commend how nicely it's  held up especially in first person mode  this game is full of surprises creepy  world building and even new enemies like  the bandersnatch a rejected warped  tyrant that can slap your face from  across the room fortunately this game is  pretty damn accessible it's available on  just about everything from the xbox  series x original dreamcast version and  everything in between almost too many  options honestly the original dreamcast  version is simply called resident evil  code veronica but everything after that  is the special edition called code  veronica x it's got a few more  pre-rendered cutscenes and even a new  haircut for steve for some reason i  originally played it on the playstation  2 and when they released an hd version  in 2011 i wanted in after downloading it  and reliving this awesome experience  once again i was surprised to learn that  i played through the ps2 port and not  the hd version idiot so if you're gonna  dive in and you'd prefer the updated  aspect ratio and smoother textures be  sure to look out for that hd badge  whatever even after accidentally playing  through the ps2 port i still had an  awesome time or three aspect ratio and  all  now that i've gushed about this game for  all the world to hear i have a  confession i never played resident evil  zero i played the intro on a friend's  copy but never made it past the opening  train sequence while i generally know  what happens in the game story i know  i'm missing out big time if you've made  it to this point in the video tell me if  you think i should give it another shot  i mean i just spilled my guts over a 20  year old game i think i can do it again  thanks for watching  you

